# Ex6b  cluster of 128 water molecules cut from ice, 400 K, Nose-Hoover chain thermostat
# (b) semi-empirical MD, GFN2-xTB (ORCA calls the bundled otool_xtb), large cluster
# 5000 steps x 0.5 fs = 2500 fs. The ORCA manual recommends a time step of at most 0.5 fs
# for systems containing hydrogen.
#
# Cell Sphere cx, cy, cz, r: soft harmonic wall that keeps molecules evaporating from the hot cluster
# from flying away. "Sphere of size 50 A" is read as diameter 50 A -> r = 25 A. The centre is the
# geometric centre of the cluster (the xyz is not centred at the origin); the cluster itself has a
# radius of only 13.7 A, so the wall acts only on molecules that leave the cluster.
! MD XTB2

%md
  Timestep   0.5_fs
  Initvel    400_K
  Thermostat NHC 400_K Timecon 10.0_fs
  Cell       Sphere 3.802, 6.585, 7.322, 25.0
  Dump       Position Stride 1 Filename "ex6b_trajectory_XTB.xyz"
  Run        5000
end

* xyzfile 0 1 ../ex6b_water_cluster_128H2O_for_XTB.xyz
